-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC #### A1.2 Life with UC
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Unity Catalog fundamentally transforms Databricks’ data governance model by replacing the legacy Hive metastore’s per-workspace, cluster-scoped architecture with a centralized, account-level metadata repository. Unlike the legacy model—where each workspace managed its own metastore, siloing access controls and data governance locally—Unity Catalog enables unified management of databases, tables, views, and files across all workspaces. This shift delivers robust cross-workspace security, centralized auditing, streamlined permission assignment to account-level users and groups, and simplifies compliance. Organizations benefit from comprehensive governance, standardized policies, and seamless data sharing that were previously impractical with the legacy Hive metastore’s fragmented structure.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Remember that UC metastores are subject to the following constraints:
-- MAGIC - You can have only one metastore per region; it cannot be directly used across regions (although OpenSharing can provide a read-only bridge across regions/clouds).  
-- MAGIC - A workspace must be attached to a UC metastore to use UC features.  
-- MAGIC - Each workspace can attach to only one UC metastore at a time, but a single metastore can be assigned to many workspaces (within the same region).
-- MAGIC - Metastores provide regional isolation, but data isolation typically begins at the catalog level, not at the metastore.  
-- MAGIC
